window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Hunters are coming out of the shadows.</p> <p>There are new enemies on the horizon, and the war is growing larger every day.</p> <p>For centuries, vampires have lived among humans in secret until one press conference threatens the livelihood of bloodsuckers worldwide, including my inhuman children. I dare my adversaries to come anywhere near them. But I can’t fight alone. I need my powerful vampire husband at my side.</p> <p>But the Council of Elders is up in arms, ancient vampires, whose only course of action against this threat is to use Sam Mason as a scapegoat. Now Sam’s own kind is hunting him, forcing us to separate into two camps to keep our family safe.</p> <p>To make matters worse, my deranged sister, Rianne, has thrown down the gauntlet. The only way to deal with her is fight to the death. I have no plans to die, but fate has a twisted sense of humor.</p> <p>The Prodigies is book five in the continuing saga in this enemies-to-lovers paranormal romance featuring Sam &amp; Layla. Their story is rife with action, suspense, snarky banter, a slow-burn romance that’s sure to singe your earbuds and ends on a cliffhanger. This is an ongoing series that begins in The Hunted. For a better listening experience, the books should be listened to in order.</p> <p>Series Listening Order:</p> <p>1. The Hunted</p> <p>2. The Predator</p> <p>3. The Union</p> <p>4. The Dawning</p> <p>5. The Prodigies</p> <p>6. The Prophecy</p> <p>7. The Rebirth</p>"; 
